https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aerb-approves-first-approach-to-criticality-for-rapp-8-in-rajasthan/articleshow/136004429.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136004429.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aerb-approves-first-approach-to-criticality-for-rapp-8-in-rajasthan/articleshow/136004429.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aerb-approves-first-approach-to-criticality-for-rapp-8-in-rajasthan/articleshow/136004429.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-20T02:08:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Srinivas Laxman</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136004438,imgsize-84170.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UNFPA puts India's population at 1.47 billion in 2026, calls for investment in 'youth dividend']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/unfpa-puts-indias-population-at-1-47-billion-in-2026-calls-for-investment-in-youth-dividend/articleshow/136004405.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136004405.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The UNFPA report forecasts that India's population could reach 1.7 billion by 2066. Currently, over 25% of Indians are aged 10 to 24, showcasing a substantial youth presence. This necessitates urgent investments in youth services and reproductive health to fulfill their future aspirations. Despite economic concerns, young individuals exhibit remarkable optimism, reflecting evolving societal norms and women's choices regarding family size.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/unfpa-puts-indias-population-at-1-47-billion-in-2026-calls-for-investment-in-youth-dividend/articleshow/13600440