zed the need for international cooperation in the fight against terrorism and organized crime, specifically calling for the return of offenders hiding abroad. He pointed out important milestones, such as the dismantling of the Popular Front of India network. The ongoing two-day Anti-Terror Conference aims to foster intelligence sharing and strengthen investigations, ultimately enhancing inter-agency collaboration to tackle evolving security threats.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bring-them-back-to-end-terror-amit-shah-pushes-to-hunt-down-fugitives-hiding-abroad/articleshow/135995196.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bring-them-back-to-end-terror-amit-shah-pushes-to-hunt-down-fugitives-hiding-abroad/articleshow/135995196.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T19:50:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135995323,imgsize-42250.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mahadev betting app case: Kingpin Saurabh Chandrakar sent to judicial custody till December 2]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mahadev-betting-app-case-kingpin-saurabh-chandrakar-sent-to-judicial-custody-till-december-2/articleshow/135993498.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135993498.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Saurabh Chandrakar has been sent to judicial custody until December 2 by a special court in Raipur. The Enforcement Directorate indicated that it does not require further custodial interrogation at this point. Chandrakar was extradited from Oman earlier this month and produced before the court after a CBI operation. Allegations suggest he operated an illegal online betting network earning significant amounts monthly since 2020.]]></description><link><![CD